1
00:04:19,354 --> 00:04:25,354
Love is a force of nature.

2
00:08:38,709 --> 00:08:44,709
Brokeback Mountain is a drama, romance film directed by Ang Lee.

3
00:12:58,064 --> 00:13:04,064
In 1960s Wyoming, two men develop a strong emotional and sexual relationship that endures as a lifelong
connection complicating their lives as they get married and start families of their own.

4
00:17:17,419 --> 00:17:23,419
Ennis Del Mar, played by Heath Ledger.

5
00:21:36,774 --> 00:21:42,774
Jack Twist, played by Jake Gyllenhaal.

6
00:25:56,129 --> 00:26:02,129
Alma Beers, played by Michelle Williams.

7
00:30:15,483 --> 00:30:21,483
Lureen Newsome, played by Anne Hathaway.

8
00:34:34,838 --> 00:34:40,838
Joe Aguirre, played by Randy Quaid.

9
00:38:54,193 --> 00:39:00,193
Cassie Cartwright, played by Linda Cardellini.

10
00:43:13,548 --> 00:43:19,548
Brokeback Mountain is a 2005 American neo-Western romantic drama film
directed by Ang Lee and produced by Diana Ossana and James Schamus.

11
00:47:32,903 --> 00:47:38,903
Adapted from the 1997 short story by Annie Proulx, the
screenplay was written by Ossana and Larry McMurtry.

12
00:51:52,258 --> 00:51:58,258
The film stars Heath Ledger, Jake Gyllenhaal, Anne
Hathaway, and Michelle Williams.

13
00:56:11,612 --> 00:56:17,612
Its plot depicts the complex romantic relationship between two American cowboys,
Ennis Del Mar and Jack Twist, in the American West from 1963 to 1983.

14
01:00:30,967 --> 01:00:36,967
Lee became attached to the project in 2001 after previous attempts to
adapt Proulx's story into a film did not materialize.

15
01:04:50,322 --> 01:04:56,322
Focus Features and River Road Entertainment would
jointly produce and distribute the film.

16
01:09:09,677 --> 01:09:15,677
After Ledger and Gyllenhaal's casting was announced in 2003, filming
commenced in various locations in Alberta in 2004.

17
01:13:29,032 --> 01:13:35,032
Brokeback Mountain premiered at the 2005 Venice International Film Festival, where it won
the Golden Lion, and was released to theaters on December 9 that year.

18
01:17:48,387 --> 01:17:54,387
The film received widespread critical acclaim, with high praise
for the performances of Ledger and Gyllenhaal.

19
01:22:07,741 --> 01:22:13,741
It emerged as a commercial success at the box-office, grossing over $178 million
worldwide against its $14 million budget, and won various accolades.

20
01:26:27,096 --> 01:26:33,096
At the 78th Academy Awards, Brokeback Mountain was nominated for Best Picture and
won for Best Director, Best Adapted Screenplay, and Original Score.

21
01:30:46,451 --> 01:30:52,451
It garnered seven nominations at the 63rd Golden Globe Awards, winning Best
Motion Picture — Drama, Best Director, Best Screenplay and Best Song.

22
01:35:05,806 --> 01:35:11,806
At the 59th British Academy Film Awards, Brokeback Mountain had nine nominations, winning Best
Film, Best Direction, Best Adapted Screenplay and Best Supporting Actor (Gyllenhaal).

23
01:39:25,161 --> 01:39:31,161
It was the film that topped the best of the year lists.

24
01:43:44,516 --> 01:43:50,516
Brokeback Mountain was subject to controversies; its loss to Crash (2004) for the Academy Award for Best Picture,
subsequent censorship, and criticism from conservative media outlets received significant attention.

25
01:48:03,870 --> 01:48:09,870
The sexuality of the main characters has been subject to discussion.

26
01:52:23,225 --> 01:52:29,225
Brokeback Mountain has also been regarded as a turning point for
the advancement of queer cinema into the mainstream.

27
01:56:42,580 --> 01:56:48,580
In 2018, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically, or
aesthetically significant" and was listed on the ballot for the American Film Institute's list of AFI's 100 Years...100 Movies (10th Anniversary Edition).

28
02:01:01,935 --> 02:01:07,935
Since then, it has been ranked by several publications, film critics and scholars as
one of the best films of the 2000s, the 21st century and of all time.

29
02:05:21,290 --> 02:05:27,290
The film explores themes of secret love, wyoming, usa,
countryside, homophobia, marriage crisis.

30
02:09:40,645 --> 02:09:46,645
The tone is emotional.
